Health."},"laws":[],"number":"2245","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"B001298","district":2,"fullName":"Rep. Bacon, Don [R-NE-2]","party":"R","state":"NE"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-03-21","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Autonomy for Disabled Veterans Act</strong></p><p>This bill increases the maximum amount authorized under the Home Improvements and Structural Alterations (HISA) grant program to $10,000 for veterans with a service-connected disability and $5,000 for those with disabilities that are not service-connected. The HISA grant program provides medically necessary improvements and structural alterations to a veteran's (or service member's) primary residence for specified purposes (e.g., allowing for entrance to their home).</p><p>The bill requires the Department of Veterans Affairs to increase the maximum dollar amount of the grant in accordance with inflation as determined by the Consumer Price Index.</p>","updateDate":"2025-06-25T15:13:01Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Autonomy for Disabled Veterans Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-07-23T08:09:19Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-07-23T08:09:19Z"}
